{"result":"{
  "id": "18485",
  "key": "SFCC-250",
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "*Standard Cart Interaction*\n\n# Given a Shopper has a variant in their cart and the quantity equals the configured maximum of 3, when the cart renders, then the + control for that line item is disabled and visually greyed out while the – control remains enabled.\n# Given a Shopper has a variant in their cart and the quantity equals the configured maximum of 3, when the cart renders, then an inline warning message is displayed beneath the quantity stepper reading \"Maximum purchase quantity reached for this size\" with an info icon (see [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-795|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-795|smart-link] )\n# Given the maximum quantity limit is reached, when the cart renders, then a page-level warning banner is displayed at the top of the cart drawer reading \"An item in your bag has reached maximum quantity\" (see [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-404|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-404|smart-link] )\n# Given the maximum quantity limit is reached, when the Shopper views the Checkout CTA, then the button remains enabled — maximum quantity alone does not block checkout. Apple Pay and Google Pay express buttons also remain enabled.\n\n*Cart Merge*\n\n# Given a Guest Shopper has items in their cart and signs in to an account where the combined quantity of the same SKU exceeds the maximum limit of 3, when sign-in completes and the baskets merge, then the quantity is automatically capped at 3 — it never displays a quantity exceeding the maximum.\n# Given the merged quantity has been automatically capped at the maximum of 3, when the cart renders post-merge, then the + control on the affected line item is disabled and visually greyed out while the – control remains enabled.\n# Given the merged quantity has been automatically capped at the maximum of 3, when the cart renders post-merge, then an inline warning message is displayed beneath the affected line item reading \"Maximum purchase quantity reached for this size\" with an info icon  (see [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-795|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-795|smart-link] )\n# Given the merged quantity has been automatically capped at the maximum of 3, when the cart renders post-merge, then a page-level warning banner is displayed at the top of the cart drawer reading \"An item in your bag has reached maximum quantity\" (see [https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-404|https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-404|smart-link] )\n# Given the merged quantity has been automatically capped at the maximum of 3, when the Shopper views the Checkout CTA, then the button remains enabled — the auto-cap resolves the quantity issue and checkout is not blocked. Apple Pay and Google Pay express buttons also remain enabled."
  }
}"}

